    "_rawMissionName": "False Alarm",
    "_rawMissionDescription": "Chain Home has plotted another raid inbound. It is the fourth today and the last three were nothing at all - the station has a fault the technicians have not found yet. Sector will not stand the squadron down on a maybe. Scramble, look, and come back tired.",
    "_rawIntelThreatReport": "A plot on the screen and nothing behind it, most likely. Most likely is not certainly, which is the whole problem.",
    "_rawApTransmission": "On the vector, climbing through eight thousand. Visibility good. Nothing on the horizon.",
    "_rawGwTransmission": "Vectored into cloud at angels ten. Cannot see a thing and the plot has moved again.",
    "_rawApSuccessTransmission": "Sector empty - but we swept it properly, and Sector has the report to prove the plot was false. That fault gets fixed tonight.",
    "_rawApFailureTransmission": "Nothing there. Again. Two hours of fuel and four tired pilots for a ghost on a screen.",
    "_rawGwSuccessTransmission": "Came down through the cloud in the wrong county, worked our way back, and confirmed the sector was clear. Something to show for it, at least.",
    "_rawGwFailureTransmission": "Chased a phantom through cloud until the fuel ran low. The crews are past exhausted and Chain Home is still broken.",
